WEBVTT

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:03.290
<i>It's March.</i>

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:08.480
<i>It'll soon be a full year since 
I first came to Kura.</i>

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.740
<i>We've been invited by 
Rikyu-kun's father who lives in Tokyo,</i>

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.240
<i>Kirishima Sakyo-san,</i>

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:19.370
<i>to visit the estate of 
Rikyu-kun's grandfather</i>

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.720
<i>in one of Kyoto's leading high-end 
residential districts, Takagamine.</i>

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.760
<i>Sakyo-san and Yoshie-san are divorced,</i>

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.740
<i>and I've heard he was a bad husband,</i>

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:31.200
<i>but he actually seems very 
funny and personable.</i>

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.060
Hey, Kiyotaka-kun, Aoi-san.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.140
Thank you for coming today.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.730
It's nothing.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.890
What is Rikyu-kun's grandfather like?

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:46.320
I don't see him often myself, 
but the Saito family is pretty loaded...

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.150
Their mansion's full of expensive-looking
 art pieces and everything.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.910
And Sakyo-san and all his brothers 
have been called there?

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:58.320
Dad's invitation said,

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:04.660
"For those with no faith in their own eyes,
 bring an appraiser with you."

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:11.110
Rikyu spoke highly of him, 
so I decided to ask Kiyotaka-kun first.

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:12.920
Sorry, Kiyo-nii.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:14.680
Don't mention it.

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:16.840
It's a request as an appraiser, after all.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:18.930
I couldn't ask for more.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>I see...</i>

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.470
Of course, Aoi-san didn't need to come, too.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.190
You could've left her watching the store.

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.400
Well, it does sort of feel 
like a family thing...

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:36.560
Looking at beautiful things 
will help you hone your eye.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.950
I'm sure it will be a good 
learning experience for you, Aoi-san.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.780
Beautiful things?

00:01:42.980 --> 00:01:44.000
What is it?

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:46.710
O-Oh, nothing!

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.500
I'll do my best!

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:55.460
"Conditions of an Heir"

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:55.460
Episode 12

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:02.780
This way, please.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.230
Tsukasa, Kazuhiko.

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:10.940
It's been a while, eh?

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.900
Hey, Big Bro.

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:14.480
It has been a while.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:16.890
<i>I heard they were brothers,</i>

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:19.350
<i>but the three of them 
don't look anything alike...</i>

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.230
They really don't, do they?

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:23.990
Holmes-san!

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:26.520
We can't exactly hide it.

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:29.010
They all have different mothers.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:31.440
I see.

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.720
I suspect that has something to do 
with the gathering here today...

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:37.620
Well, if it isn't Kiyotaka!

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:41.610
Keiko-san! It's been so long.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.700
You're back in Japan?

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.880
Yes, and I'm so happy to see you!

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.300
Aoi-san, this is Fujiwara Keiko-san.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.760
She's the curator of an 
art museum in New York.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:03.030
Curator?

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:06.290
It's a bit like a museum's manager.

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:11.580
I see. So she's the appraiser 
you brought, Kazuhiko?

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.920
What about you, Tsukasa?

00:03:13.130 --> 00:03:15.400
They're running a little late.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.420
But I asked a connoisseur 
who's any appraiser's equal.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.480
<i>A connoisseur who's any appraiser's equal?</i>

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.320
<i>I wonder who that could be...</i>

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:25.430
Oh?

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:26.920
Look at this!

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:28.460
What is it?

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.280
The hanging wisteria crest!

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:37.440
I believe it's seen often in 
Fujiwara and Saito families.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.200
Impressive as ever. 
My family crest is the same one!

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:45.810
Dad.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.740
Sakyo, Tsukasa, Kazuhiko, and Rikyu.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.210
Thank you all for coming.

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:54.850
It's nice to meet you all as well.

00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:58.710
I am the head of House Saito, Saito Ukon.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.870
You appraisers...

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.020
Miss, what are you here for?

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:07.470
Oh? Um...

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:11.730
I'm the one who invited her, Dad.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:17.330
The only people I want to see 
right now are my sons and appraisers.

00:04:17.330 --> 00:04:19.370
I'm sorry, miss.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:22.240
I don't believe you have a place here.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:25.360
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.490
I'm Yagashira Kiyotaka.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.560
Oh, you must be Seiji-san's...

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.040
This is Mashiro Aoi-san, a member of my staff.

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.280
She's an apprentice appraiser, like me.

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.380
I remember!

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:43.510
She's the one who won the appraising 
game at Yanagihara-sensei's party.

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.260
I took part in that, too!

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.520
Ukon-san, Aoi-san has a very good eye.

00:04:51.760 --> 00:04:55.770
It would be inaccurate to say 
that she has no place here.

00:04:56.200 --> 00:04:57.470
Holmes-san...

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:03.030
Well then, Aoi-san...

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:06.340
Let us test you.

00:05:12.840 --> 00:05:14.220
Excuse me.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:17.540
These are...

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.800
Raku tea bowls... Amazing.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:28.850
You know there are many makers 
of Raku tea bowls, I'm sure.

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:29.550
Yes.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:35.310
Then tell me who made 
each of these tea bowls.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:40.060
Some of them may have even been made 
by those outside of the House of Raku.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.580
That's fine.

00:05:42.410 --> 00:05:44.620
If it's Raku ware, I can handle it.

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.900
Okay, I'm going to get started.

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.020
I think these two are the ninth heir 
to the House of Raku, Ryonyu.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:02.480
This one is the fourth heir, Ichinyu.

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:04.440
This is the fourteenth heir, Kakunyu.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.380
This one is the fifteenth heir, Kichizaemon.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.970
And this last one...

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:17.230
This is by the man still known as the art's 
greatest master, the third heir, Donyu.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:21.230
<i>Hmm, no...</i>

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.360
I'm sorry, let me take that back.

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:29.110
Is it... Hon'ami Koetsu?

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.590
U-Um... Was I wrong?

00:06:35.170 --> 00:06:37.620
I'm sorry. I'll get ready to go...

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.620
Magnificent!

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:45.710
Aoi-san, forgive my earlier rudeness.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:47.880
I'm very sorry.

00:06:48.480 --> 00:06:50.630
You truly are remarkable!

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:52.460
O-Oh, no...

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.420
Holmes-san taught me all that,

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:57.640
and I almost got the last one wrong...

00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.090
Not so fast, Aoi-san.

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.770
It's said that the third heir, Donyu,
 worked closely with Koetsu

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.400
and was greatly influenced by him.

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.850
The fact that you mistook it for Donyu's work

00:07:09.850 --> 00:07:11.800
and then immediately realized it was Koetsu's

00:07:11.800 --> 00:07:13.540
speaks incredibly well of you.

00:07:13.540 --> 00:07:15.350
Really?

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:18.420
Goodness, she's a formidable one.

00:07:19.690 --> 00:07:21.420
She might be your rival 
soon enough, Keiko-san.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:27.300
Anyway, I'd like to treat 
you as a proper appraiser.

00:07:27.560 --> 00:07:29.930
Why don't you pair up with Rikyu?

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.240
With me?

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:32.550
Pair up?

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:38.010
Tsukasa, your partner doesn't 
seem to be here yet...

00:07:38.010 --> 00:07:40.560
Pardon my tardy arrival.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:46.320
Tsukasa-san invited me.

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.570
My name is Tanaka Hiroshi.

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.120
Tanaka?

00:07:52.340 --> 00:07:55.570
You're late, Tanaka. What were you doing?

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:59.580
Well, you had such a fun little 
diversion goin' on in here,

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.250
I thought might watch from outside.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:08.780
Seems the little lady here's got quite an eye.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:14.720
Well, we're short on time, so I'll get to it.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:18.010
I brought you all here for one reason:

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.720
to determine a successor 
for the House of Saito.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.730
My wife passed when she was young,

00:08:26.070 --> 00:08:29.230
so in order to keep the warrior 
House of Saito from dying out,

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:33.050
I had the three of you 
with different mothers

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:34.550
and let them raise you.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.640
But you all have your merits and demerits,

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.370
so I don't know how best 
to pick an appropriate successor.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:45.010
That's why, rather than choosing based
 on appropriateness for House Saito,

00:08:45.010 --> 00:08:49.380
I've decided to choose the heir 
who best understands House Saito.

00:08:49.830 --> 00:08:52.630
There are many treasures in this mansion.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:59.140
The one able to determine the greatest
 to House Saito will be made my successor.

00:08:59.340 --> 00:09:03.360
As for you appraisers, don't tell them 
any more than they need to know.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:07.150
It's up to my sons to find their own answers.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:09.900
Those are my conditions.

00:09:10.220 --> 00:09:13.150
I want to hear your answers 
by 7:00 this evening.

00:09:13.390 --> 00:09:15.530
Now, begin!

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.410
<i>That afternoon, we went around appraising 
the treasures of House Saito.</i>

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.180
<i>In the traditional room on the first floor,</i>

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:26.670
<i>I saw a powerful ink painting 
of pines on a sliding screen.</i>

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:32.050
<i>Holmes-san seemed interested in it, 
but it was apparently unsigned.</i>

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:36.090
<i>There were amazing folding 
screens and vases, too.</i>

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:45.430
<i>We then passed by a grand mirror 
on the staircase landing</i>

00:09:45.430 --> 00:09:47.190
<i>on our way to the second floor hall</i>

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:50.400
<i>where we saw what had to be the most 
expensive things in the house:</i>

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:52.960
<i>a Qing Dynasty cloisonné vase,</i>

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.570
<i>a Bizen Osafune Chikakage sword,</i>

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.080
<i>and a Joseon white porcelain vase</i>

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:00.850
<i>that Ensho took immediate interest in.</i>

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:06.260
<i>These objects far surpassed 
anything else in the mansion.</i>

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:16.770
<i>I'm sure everyone thinks something in that 
hall is the Saito family's greatest treasure...</i>

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:21.160
<i>This is really tough.</i>

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:23.060
It's Aoi-san, isn't it?

00:10:23.710 --> 00:10:25.030
You must be tired.

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:27.480
Can I sit next to you?

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:28.780
Help yourself.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:35.340
Your eye for appraisal 
really took me by surprise.

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:37.360
It's amazing to have that 
at such a young age.

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:41.990
Oh, no. It's only because 
Holmes-san has been teaching me...

00:10:42.250 --> 00:10:44.990
Oh? Kiyotaka has, huh?

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:48.520
Um, are the two of you close?

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.000
We've known each other for several years.

00:10:53.550 --> 00:10:56.510
We first met when Seiji-san came to New York,

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:58.360
and we immediately hit it off.

00:10:58.360 --> 00:11:00.130
He even came to spend the night with me!

00:11:01.340 --> 00:11:03.010
S-Spend the night?

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:05.920
Yes. That silly Kiyotaka...

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:09.020
The entire time he was at my apartment,
 we barely slept at all.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:13.910
S-Sorry, I'd better get back to Rikyu-kun!

00:11:20.290 --> 00:11:22.220
<i>Why did she say that to me?</i>

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:25.030
<i>Does she want me to stay 
away from Holmes-san?</i>

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.360
<i>I get it...</i>

00:11:27.360 --> 00:11:29.620
<i>I already drew a line.</i>

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:33.370
<i>I said I wouldn't fall 
any further for Holmes-san.</i>

00:11:33.370 --> 00:11:35.540
Aoi-san, are you all right?

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.860
I thought I'd try imitatin' him.

00:11:40.860 --> 00:11:42.800
Did I do that well?

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:48.060
Is something the matter, Aoi-san?

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.220
S-Stay away!

00:11:51.790 --> 00:11:55.320
Say, you're Holmes-han's woman, ain't ya?

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:58.940
What you did at New Year's was right funny...

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:03.500
I figured you'd defend him,

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.830
but you gave us both a good tongue-lashin'.

00:12:07.230 --> 00:12:11.580
You're such an unremarkable little thing,
 I'd wondered why he'd want ya...

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.320
But you're not bad at all.

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:15.060
Y-You've got it all wrong!

00:12:15.060 --> 00:12:16.840
We haven't done anything...

00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.160
What's all this, now?

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:20.840
You're a virgin, eh?

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:22.650
Wh-What?

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:27.390
If that insatiable, forceful man 
ain't laid a hand on you yet,

00:12:27.390 --> 00:12:30.100
he must really value you.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:33.390
Though maybe you're putting too 
high a premium on yourself...

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:35.100
He'll be gettin' rid of you soon enough.

00:12:43.920 --> 00:12:46.110
Calling yourself Tanaka...

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.560
Ooh, scary.

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:49.740
You sure are one violent little brat.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:54.920
The force of your incredible 
rudeness caused my foot to slip.

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.120
Holmes-san...

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.610
That was one awful big slip.

00:12:58.610 --> 00:13:02.130
And they seem to get more forceful 
when that girl's involved.

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:04.990
You seem to be under the wrong impression.

00:13:04.990 --> 00:13:07.830
Aoi-san and I are not dating.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:12.140
Because, as you said, I am an 
insatiable and forceful man.

00:13:13.330 --> 00:13:15.890
Yeah, that sure adds up.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.400
Hey, Tanaka!

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:20.400
Don't go running off without me!

00:13:20.400 --> 00:13:24.150
I paid you a ton for this, 
so do your damn job!

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:24.150
Seems I'm bein' called away.

00:13:26.280 --> 00:13:28.480
Aoi-san, are you all right?

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:30.860
Did he do anything to you?

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.540
I-I'm fine...

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:34.990
He just said some rude things, that's all.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:40.170
That man's offensiveness knows no limit.

00:13:40.920 --> 00:13:44.670
But the things he said... He had a point.

00:13:45.080 --> 00:13:46.460
A point?

00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:50.430
The truth is, before I moved to Kyoto...

00:13:54.400 --> 00:14:00.390
My old boyfriend might have dumped 
me because I was too prudish.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.730
I loved him, so I've always wondered...

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:10.530
Why did I act like that?

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.020
You're wrong.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:15.830
You haven't done anything wrong.

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:19.710
Human relations all come down to karma.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:23.170
That wasn't something you 
could have done anything about.

00:14:23.780 --> 00:14:27.730
So please... don't blame yourself 
for it any longer.

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:34.390
Holmes-san...

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:40.480
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have 
embraced you like that...

00:14:40.680 --> 00:14:42.890
N-No, it's fine...

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:47.040
I really am sorry.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:51.080
When humans get desperate, 
they can do outrageous things, I suppose...

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:52.240
Desperate?

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:56.750
Well, I... I didn't want you to cry, so...

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.000
I'll hear your answers now.

00:15:05.190 --> 00:15:08.760
I dropped out, so I pass, of course.

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:13.260
Kazuhiko, you chose the cloisonné vase?

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:18.020
Yes. Because I thought it was the 
most valuable item in the house.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.770
And Tsukasa, you chose the sword?

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:22.000
Yes.

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:26.020
The sword should be the pride 
of the warriors of House Saito.

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:30.780
Sakyo, your sheet is blank. Why?

00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:36.280
The mirror on the landing. 
When I saw it, I realized...

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:41.290
Perhaps we ourselves, reflected in that mirror,
 are House Saito's greatest treasure.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.550
I told you to look 
for an object, not a person.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.870
It's not something so ridiculous!

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:54.960
Really?

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:56.550
I'm so embarrassed!

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.560
Dad...

00:15:58.840 --> 00:15:59.650
In that case...

00:15:59.650 --> 00:16:00.430
Is it me?

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.070
You're both insufficient!

00:16:02.070 --> 00:16:05.000
You all fail the test to become my successor!

00:16:07.050 --> 00:16:08.420
The real answer is...

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.070
Holmes-san?

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:16.470
Kiyotaka-kun seems to know the answer.

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:18.080
Would you care to enlighten us?

00:16:18.770 --> 00:16:20.580
Certainly. If I may...

00:16:21.180 --> 00:16:25.580
The treasure of House Saito 
is what that sword symbolizes.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.890
This crest on its scabbard is a bellflower.

00:16:28.890 --> 00:16:32.560
It's different from the Saito clan's
 hanging wisteria crest.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:36.340
In other words, that sword was a gift.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:41.040
The bellflower crest is associated with 
the famous general Akechi Mitsuhide.

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:46.350
It struck me that the Saitos might 
be descendants of Saito Toshimitsu,

00:16:46.350 --> 00:16:49.360
the important and dedicated 
retainer of Mitsuhide.

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:52.980
Even Mitsuhide, who went down 
in history as a traitor,

00:16:52.980 --> 00:16:55.330
was an important lord to this house.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:57.890
That sword embodies the sentiment,

00:16:57.890 --> 00:17:01.240
"We owe our very existence 
to Lord Mitsuhide."

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:07.750
That is what makes it such 
a unique treasure to House Saito.

00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:10.170
That's right, Kiyotaka-kun.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:15.260
If you were my grandson, I would choose 
you as my successor without hesitation.

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.010
Oh, I would hardly...

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:27.260
Thanks for today, Aoi-san.

00:17:27.260 --> 00:17:30.120
I'm sorry I've been so mean.

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:32.190
Oh, it's all right...

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:39.530
Ever since I met you, I've felt 
like I lost my place at Kura.

00:17:40.040 --> 00:17:44.040
I felt like you'd stolen everything 
that was important to me.

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.270
Rikyu-kun...

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:54.800
But today, you made it clear that you're 
working hard to earn your place at Kura.

00:17:55.290 --> 00:17:57.180
So I'm going to acknowledge you.

00:17:58.120 --> 00:17:59.800
Acknowledge me?

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:02.490
As my successor.

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:07.860
Th-Thank you, Rikyu-kun.

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:12.210
Holmes.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:17.320
What do you think is the most 
valuable treasure in this house?

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.320
Good question.

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:21.820
The white porcelain, right?

00:18:21.820 --> 00:18:23.560
No, not that.

00:18:23.560 --> 00:18:24.580
What?

00:18:25.020 --> 00:18:27.330
The screen painting on the first floor.

00:18:27.740 --> 00:18:31.330
I believe it to be the work
 of Tawaraya Sotatsu,

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:33.410
painter of the <i>Wind God</i> 
and <i>Thunder God</i> screens.

00:18:33.410 --> 00:18:35.840
I would estimate it's on
 the level of a national treasure.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.150
I see...

00:18:40.970 --> 00:18:46.100
I came here today to tease you a bit,
 but it seems I failed horribly.

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:47.340
Yes.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:51.700
Because you're incapable of understanding 
Tawaraya Sotatsu, I believe.

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:55.120
Sotatsu was a painter shrouded in mystery.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:59.990
He created many works, like that screen,
 without a seal or signature.

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:06.240
It's as if Sotatsu personally wanted 
to erase all traces of himself.

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:11.370
Meanwhile, despite creating 
counterfeits in the shadows,

00:19:11.370 --> 00:19:14.820
in truth, you burn with a 
desire to be acknowledged.

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:16.800
You're his polar opposite.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.880
Ain't no way you could understand him.

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.240
You never change, do ya?

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:24.210
That part of you really gets my goat...

00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:27.640
I loathe you to the core.

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:29.640
The feeling is mutual.

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:40.020
Aoi-san, were you listening?

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:46.910
Why do you always say things that 
rub Ensho-san the wrong way?

00:19:47.170 --> 00:19:50.160
I wanted his feelings to erupt.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:57.170
I thought doing that might help 
lift the cloud that hangs over him...

00:19:57.620 --> 00:19:59.120
But I failed, I suppose.

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:00.900
Hey...

00:20:03.010 --> 00:20:05.550
No, that's all an excuse.

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:10.060
I just find the man completely
 and utterly repugnant.

00:20:10.440 --> 00:20:13.440
If I had the talent he does...

00:20:14.900 --> 00:20:17.550
<i>Holmes-san is jealous of Ensho?</i>

00:20:18.730 --> 00:20:22.780
<i>So they're both actually 
jealous of each other...</i>

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:26.880
<i>No, not just them...</i>

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.620
Um, Holmes-san,

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.500
about Keiko-san...

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:35.050
Did you two used to go out?

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:39.210
Um, she said you spent 
the night at her house...

00:20:40.220 --> 00:20:43.720
Yes... but it was literally 
just an overnight stay.

00:20:44.600 --> 00:20:48.790
I heard that she had an amazing 
collection of rare art books,

00:20:48.790 --> 00:20:52.120
so I spent two days on the 
sofa reading them all.

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:55.650
I-Is that all it was?

00:20:57.010 --> 00:21:00.230
<i>Wait, why do I feel relieved to hear that?</i>

00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:03.510
Shall we go now, Aoi-san?

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:13.250
It really smells like spring.

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:17.000
It will soon be a year 
since you came to Kura, won't it?

00:21:18.580 --> 00:21:21.040
<i>Yeah, one full year since then...</i>

00:21:22.290 --> 00:21:26.130
<i>Meeting Holmes lifted me out of my sadness.</i>

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:31.140
<i>I decided to draw a line and 
keep my feelings a secret...</i>

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:35.140
<i>But I've been lying to myself all this time.</i>

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:36.980
<i>Because I was afraid of being hurt,</i>

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.190
<i>I made excuses and turned away...</i>

00:21:40.650 --> 00:21:43.000
<i>I've been lying to my own heart.</i>

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.280
<i>Please wait!</i>

00:21:55.800 --> 00:21:57.980
<i>I love you, Kiyotaka-san!</i>

00:21:59.810 --> 00:22:00.760
Aoi-san!

00:22:02.740 --> 00:22:05.790
The moon is beautiful tonight, isn't it?

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:11.360
Yes...

00:22:13.520 --> 00:22:15.180
It's very pretty.

00:22:17.320 --> 00:22:22.070
<i>I'm going to keep this 
feeling to myself for now.</i>

00:22:22.990 --> 00:22:27.450
<i>Because I want to treasure the 
time I spend with Kiyotaka-san,</i>

00:22:28.130 --> 00:22:29.640
<i>appreciating beautiful things.</i>

00:22:36.180 --> 00:22:38.550
<i>But some day, I'll also...</i>

00:22:42.360 --> 00:22:46.960
<i>At an antique shop called Kura 
along Kyoto's Teramachi Sanjo,</i>

00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:50.970
<i>you'll find a mysterious 
Kyoto boy called Holmes.</i>

00:22:58.280 --> 00:23:00.730
Holmes, you gotta help me!

00:23:00.950 --> 00:23:04.240
My friend, the kabuki actor, 
has gotten mixed up in a case!

00:23:04.240 --> 00:23:06.580
I am not a detective.

00:23:06.580 --> 00:23:07.990
I am an appraiser.

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:10.180
Please! You gotta help me!

00:23:12.210 --> 00:23:13.880
Let's go, Holmes-san.

00:23:13.880 --> 00:23:14.330
All right.

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:16.490
Hey, wait up!

00:23:16.690 --> 00:23:20.750
<i>This is the tale of Holmes, 
AKA Yagashira Kiyotaka...</i>

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:23.460
<i>Myself, Mashiro Aoi...</i>

00:23:27.900 --> 00:23:30.780
<i>And the quiet and beautiful story of love</i>

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:36.390
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:30.780 --> 00:23:32.170
<i>and the cases we solved in Kyoto.</i>

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:51.400
"Thank you for watching!"

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:40.840
Kiyotaka-san, I want to 
tell you... how I feel.

00:23:40.840 --> 00:23:43.880
Aoi-san... let me say it.

00:23:44.600 --> 00:23:47.200
<i>Holmes of Kyoto</i>.

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:50.190
Holmes-san, you really are nasty.
